      "title": "Operator notes — span status vs HTTP",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 1 },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "code": { "language": "markdown", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false },
        "content": "## How to read these panels\n\n| Signal | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| **HTTP route spans** (FastAPI auto-instrumentation) | **HTTP status** is the response code. Span **ERROR** status usually means an unhandled exception; 4xx/5xx can still appear with OK span status depending on framework mapping — compare panels. |\n| **Manual Dirijor spans** (`dirijor.consensus`, `dirijor.terraform.subprocess`, `dirijor.realm.spin_job`, …) | Use **span status** (`ERROR` vs `OK`) for operation failure. |\n| **Wrapper** | `dirijor.wrapper.tools.invoke` — same rule: span status + HTTP on the route span. |\n\n**Realm filter:** variables `$service` and `$realm_id` apply TraceQL regex on `resource.service.name` and `span.dirijor.realm_id` where the attribute exists. Some spans (e.g. `/consensus` without `realm_id`) will not match a specific realm filter.\n\n**Latency:** Trace panels list duration per trace. Aggregate histograms require Tempo **metrics generator** + Prometheus (or Grafana Cloud) — see `docs/observability/README.md`.\n",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Documentation",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 6 },
